hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1587","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Ahmad bin Muni’ told us, saying: Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: And do not say your prayer loudly, nor be silent in it. Surat Al-Isra, verse 110. He said: “It was revealed while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was hidden.” In Mecca, when he led his Companions in prayer, he would recite the Qur’an out loud.” Al-Durqi said: “He raised his voice with the Qur’an,” and they said: “So when the polytheists heard, They cursed the Qur’an, and whoever sent it down, and whoever brought it. Then God said to his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: And do not recite Surah Al-Isra ayat 110 out loud in your prayer, that is, by your recitation. Then the polytheists will hear and curse the Qur’an, and do not fear it, Surah Al-Isra, Verse 110, from your companions, but they will not listen, but seek in the midst of that a way. Surah Al-Isra, Verse 110 110\. Al-Durqi said: “About your friends"," so do not listen to them.” Abu Bakr said: This report is of the type that I learned in the Book of Faith"," that the name may apply to some parts of a thing with parts. And the people"," God Almighty has assigned the name of prayer to the recitation in it only"," and do not recite your prayer out loud"," Surah Al-Isra"," verse 110. He meant the recitation in it"," not the prayer. All of them"," reading only"""
